<title>USA: Total World president/COO takes CEO post.</title>
<headline>Total World president/COO takes CEO post.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total World Telecommunications Inc said Friday that Donald Booth, its president and chief operating officer, had been named chief executive officer.</p>
<p>Booth succeeds Joseph Lents, who resigned as CEO but continues as chairman.  </p>
<p>The company also said John Loveridge and Denning Loveridge had resigned as members of its board. It said it had begun looking for people to replace them.</p>
<p>Total World is divesting two units and relocating its offices to Houston from Boca Raton, Fla.</p>
</text>
